=== entry ca3eb4519e0a
kind: translation
rules: invoke
intent: The skill tells the agent to follow ketchup, so it names the **ketchup** skill (keeping the link). The window sentence refers to the command the user typed, which is `/` in Claude Code and `$` in Codex, so it gives both spellings of each command; no rule covers a reference to a past invocation, so this is the closest faithful version. Keep the window rule, the read-only exception, the reply's parts, and the render-failure fallback.
--- upstream
Follow [`/ketchup`](../ketchup/SKILL.md), but show what happened in a short subtitled video instead of its summary and visuals. Its window starts at the last message the user wrote before `/ketchup-video`, not before any earlier `/ketchup`. Writing and rendering the video, outside the repo, is the one exception to its read-only rule. The reply is ketchup's opening sentence, the embedded video, one line naming any work left that you can do yourself, and the action items. When the video shows a call's options, call each option by the name the video gives it. If the render fails, say so in one line and give only the calls.
--- patched
Follow the [**ketchup**](../ketchup/SKILL.md) skill, but show what happened in a short subtitled video instead of its summary and visuals. Its window starts at the last message the user wrote before `/ketchup-video` or `$ketchup-video`, not before any earlier `/ketchup` or `$ketchup`. Writing and rendering the video, outside the repo, is the one exception to its read-only rule. The reply is ketchup's opening sentence, the embedded video, one line naming any work left that you can do yourself, and the action items. When the video shows a call's options, call each option by the name the video gives it. If the render fails, say so in one line and give only the calls.
